   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the general municipal law and the education law, in relation to insurance reserve funds of certain school districts",
    "basePrintNo": "S7756",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7756-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §6-n, Gen Muni L; add §3653, Ed L",
    "lawSection": "General Municipal Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7756\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the general municipal law and the education law, in\nrelation to insurance reserve funds of certain school districts\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nThe bill allows the Minisink Valley School District to maintain such a\nreserve fund and make expenditures from such reserve fund for any\nloss, claim, action or judgment for which such school district is\nauthorized or required to purchase or maintain insurance.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1: Amends paragraph (a) of subdivision 2 of section 6-n of the\nGeneral Municipal law to authorize the Minisink Valley Central School\nDistrict to create an insurance reserve fund, and such school district\nmay make expenditures from such reserve fund for any loss, claim,\naction or judgment in relation to health insurance costs.\n\nSection 2: Amends the Education law by adding a new section 3653 which\noutlines the procedures a school district must follow if they are\nestablishing an health insurance reserve fund.\n\nSection 3: Effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nIn New York State there is a shift in how school districts continue to\nprovide their services while staying within the tax cap. Health\ninsurance reserve funds are seen as beneficial for a municipal\ncorporation and so this law extends the statute for the Minisink\nValley Central School District. This legislation was requested by the\nMinisink Valley School District.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNone.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone to the state.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
